<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal inflation 0.1 pct in March.</title>
<headline>Portugal inflation 0.1 pct in March.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese consumer prices rose 0.1 percent in March after 0.2 percent in February to give year-on-year inflation of 2.5 percent after 2.9 percent previously, the National Statistics Institute (INE) said.</p>
<p>Average annual inflation, the government's yardstick, was 3.2 percent in March after 3.2 percent previously</p>
<p> PORTUGUESE INFLATION	  Mar 97	 Feb 97     Mar 96</p>
<p> Monthly CPI rise		  0.1	    0.2	  0.4</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr inflation		2.5	    2.9	  2.4</p>
<p> Average annual inflation	3.2	    3.2	  3.6</p>
<p> Index (base 100 1991)	 133.0	  132.9	129.7</p>
</text>
